From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:53:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msm8996-common: ims: fix outgoing calls and the once-per-boot
 crash

Two bugs that only showed once voice audio worked, both consequences of the
rename-and-merge the port depends on.

Outgoing calls died in createCallSession with
BadParcelableException: ClassNotFoundException: com.lge.imslegacy.ImsStreamMediaProfile.
Ims4's parcelables were com.android.ims FRAMEWORK classes, so their generated
readFromParcel passes null to readParcelable -- 'use the boot class loader' --
which resolved them. Renaming the package and merging it into the app moved
those classes into the app's dex, where the boot loader cannot see them. It
only bites framework -> Ims4, which is why incoming calls always worked and
dialling out failed instantly. Redirect readParcelable to a compat static using
the app's loader; that is strictly more capable, since the app loader delegates
to the boot one, so framework parcelables still resolve. 9 classes, 12 sites --
LG's own IM/IM3 parcelables carried the same latent bug.

And after every call LG's EAB presence agent queried CallLog for duration_video,
an LG-only column; AOSP's provider throws, EABAgent catches nothing on its own
thread, and because com.lge.ims is persistent the whole IMS process died and
restarted unable to re-register -- exactly one working call per boot. Stub the
one method to return null, which is already the caller's 'nothing to subscribe'
branch, via the new build-ims4.sh step 4.4 and ims/smali-stubs.txt. RCS presence
is parked anyway.

Verified 2026-10-06 07:52: outgoing and incoming calls, both with two-way
audio, back to back on one boot.
---
 ims/build-ims4.sh                             |  3 +++
 .../com/lge/ims/compat/TelephonyCompat.java   | 25 +++++++++++++++++++
 ims/method-redirects.txt                      |  7 ++++++
 ims/smali-stubs.txt                           | 11 ++++++++
 4 files changed, 46 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 ims/smali-stubs.txt

diff --git a/ims/build-ims4.sh b/ims/build-ims4.sh
index c9280037..063baf8b 100755
--- a/ims/build-ims4.sh
+++ b/ims/build-ims4.sh
@@ -107,6 +107,9 @@ echo "   $nreal real parcelable classes from the stock framework"
 echo ">> 4. rename com.android.ims -> com.lge.imslegacy in Ims4 + merge the legacy closure"
 python3 "$FORGE/tools/merge-legacy-classes.py" --app "$T/smali-ims4" --legacy "$T/legacy-final" --old com/android/ims --new com/lge/imslegacy --out "$T/merged"
 
+echo ">> 4.4 stub methods that depend on OEM-only framework features"
+[ -f "$HERE/smali-stubs.txt" ] && python3 "$FORGE/tools/stub-smali-method.py" "$T/merged" "$HERE/smali-stubs.txt"
+
 echo ">> 4.5 apply framework-API-drift method redirects"
 [ -f "$HERE/method-redirects.txt" ] && python3 "$FORGE/tools/apply-method-redirects.py" "$HERE/method-redirects.txt" "$T/merged"
 if [ -f "$HERE/smali-fixups.py" ]; then
diff --git a/ims/compat-java/com/lge/ims/compat/TelephonyCompat.java b/ims/compat-java/com/lge/ims/compat/TelephonyCompat.java
index fbb71c4e..23394dd1 100644
--- a/ims/compat-java/com/lge/ims/compat/TelephonyCompat.java
+++ b/ims/compat-java/com/lge/ims/compat/TelephonyCompat.java
@@ -204,4 +204,29 @@ public final class TelephonyCompat {
             return null;
         }
     }
+
+    /**
+     * Parcel.readParcelable with the app's class loader instead of the caller's.
+     *
+     * Ims4's parcelables were com.android.ims.* FRAMEWORK classes, so its generated readFromParcel
+     * passes null -- "use the boot class loader" -- and that resolved them. Renaming the package to
+     * com.lge.imslegacy and merging it into the app moved those classes into the app's dex, where
+     * the boot loader cannot see them, so every readParcelable(null) throws
+     * BadParcelableException: ClassNotFoundException. It only bites in the framework -> Ims4
+     * direction (an outgoing call's ImsCallProfile carries an ImsStreamMediaProfile), which is why
+     * incoming calls worked and dialling out failed with createCallSession().
+     *
+     * Redirecting every call is safe and strictly more capable: the app loader delegates to the
+     * boot loader, so framework parcelables still resolve.
+     */
+    public static android.os.Parcelable readParcelable(android.os.Parcel in,
+            ClassLoader ignoredCallerLoader) {
+        return in.readParcelable(TelephonyCompat.class.getClassLoader());
+    }
+
+    /** Same reasoning as readParcelable, for the Bundle variant. */
+    public static android.os.Bundle readBundle(android.os.Parcel in,
+            ClassLoader ignoredCallerLoader) {
+        return in.readBundle(TelephonyCompat.class.getClassLoader());
+    }
 }
diff --git a/ims/method-redirects.txt b/ims/method-redirects.txt
index 77291dd1..367e0031 100644
--- a/ims/method-redirects.txt
+++ b/ims/method-redirects.txt
@@ -43,3 +43,10 @@ Lcom/android/internal/telephony/ITelephonyRegistry;->notifyVoLteServiceStateChan
 # --- com.lge.ims.phone (IIMSPhone) is not a service on AOSP: hand Ims4 an in-process stand-in ---
 # IIMSPhoneGov.bindIMSPhone() -> ImsPhoneCompat; item 8 (VoPS) is what clears AoS NONETWORK+VOPS
 Lcom/android/internal/telephony/IIMSPhone$Stub;->asInterface(Landroid/os/IBinder;)Lcom/android/internal/telephony/IIMSPhone;|Lcom/lge/ims/compat/ImsPhoneCompat;->asInterface(Landroid/os/IBinder;)Lcom/android/internal/telephony/IIMSPhone;
+
+# The renamed com.lge.imslegacy parcelables are app classes now, but their generated readFromParcel
+# still passes null (the boot loader) because they used to be framework classes. Every one of those
+# reads throws ClassNotFoundException -- outgoing calls failed in createCallSession() unmarshalling
+# an ImsCallProfile's ImsStreamMediaProfile. The compat statics use the app loader, which delegates
+# to the boot loader, so framework parcelables still resolve.
+Landroid/os/Parcel;->readParcelable(Ljava/lang/ClassLoader;)Landroid/os/Parcelable;|static Lcom/lge/ims/compat/TelephonyCompat;->readParcelable(Landroid/os/Parcel;Ljava/lang/ClassLoader;)Landroid/os/Parcelable;
diff --git a/ims/smali-stubs.txt b/ims/smali-stubs.txt
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..6e8caf61
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ims/smali-stubs.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+# Methods in Ims4 that reach for something LG's framework had and AOSP does not. Applied by
+# build-ims4.sh with forge/tools/stub-smali-method.py; the return value is chosen from the CALLER's
+# harmless branch, not from the signature. A rule that stops matching is a build failure.
+
+# After every call the EAB (RCS presence) agent reacts to the call-log update and queries CallLog
+# for `duration_video`, an LG-only column. AOSP's provider throws IllegalArgumentException, EABAgent
+# catches nothing on its own thread, and because com.lge.ims is persistent the whole IMS process
+# dies and restarts unable to re-register -- exactly one working call per boot. The caller does
+# `if-eqz v2, :cond_87`, so null is already its "nothing to subscribe" path, and RCS presence is
+# parked anyway (see IMS.md "RCS").
+Lcom/lge/ims/service/eab/EABContactHelper;->CheckLastCallCapability()Ljava/lang/String;|null
